WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:03.280
Hi again! Let’s learn about CASPAR.

00:00:03.630 --> 00:00:08.530
CASPAR stands for Classification criteria for Psoriatic Arthritis.

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:12.260
It comes from a study published in 2006.

00:00:13.810 --> 00:00:17.870
Doctors use it to sort the signs of PsA into groups.

00:00:19.420 --> 00:00:21.410
Step one is a must.

00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:27.420
There has to be inflammation in a joint, in the spine, or where a tendon attaches to bone.

00:00:28.970 --> 00:00:31.990
Step two adds points for other signs.

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:34.740
There are five groups of signs.

00:00:36.290 --> 00:00:38.310
Group one is psoriasis.

00:00:38.660 --> 00:00:42.790
Psoriasis on your skin or scalp right now counts the most.

00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:50.940
If you don’t have it now, having had it in the past counts. If you never had it, psoriasis in a close family member counts.

00:00:52.490 --> 00:00:55.180
Group two is nail changes you have now.

00:00:55.530 --> 00:01:02.870
Examples are tiny dents called pitting, a nail lifting off the skin underneath, or thick buildup under the nail.

00:01:04.420 --> 00:01:09.050
Group three is a blood test called rheumatoid factor, or RF.

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:12.640
Here, a negative result is the one that counts.

00:01:14.190 --> 00:01:19.420
Group four is a whole finger or toe that is swollen, sometimes called a sausage digit.

00:01:19.770 --> 00:01:24.670
It counts if it is swollen now, or if a doctor wrote it down in the past.

00:01:26.220 --> 00:01:31.000
Group five is new bone forming right next to a joint, seen on an X-ray.

00:01:31.350 --> 00:01:34.180
A heel spur alone is not that finding.

00:01:35.730 --> 00:01:38.150
The reference adds up these points.

00:01:38.500 --> 00:01:41.380
But a score is not a home diagnosis.

00:01:41.730 --> 00:01:46.220
A doctor must look at all the findings and check for other causes.

00:01:47.770 --> 00:01:51.780
Knowing CASPAR can help you follow the conversation with your care team.

00:01:53.330 --> 00:01:55.920
Nice work! Let’s review.

00:01:56.270 --> 00:02:01.930
First, there must be inflammation in a joint, the spine, or a tendon attachment.

00:02:02.280 --> 00:02:10.270
Psoriasis, nail changes, a negative RF test, a swollen finger or toe, and new bone near a joint can add points.

00:02:10.620 --> 00:02:13.380
A score is not a home diagnosis.
